.TH JVMDUMP 1 "2026-10-28" "jvmdump 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jvmdump \- dump class files from a live HotSpot JVM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jvmdump
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPID\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jvmdump
attaches to a running HotSpot JVM through its dynamic attach socket, loads a
small JVMTI agent and writes every class file that is currently loaded to a
directory.  No Java agent, no JDK and no helper JVM are required.
.PP
Loaded classes are enumerated with \fBGetLoadedClasses\fR and their bytes are
obtained with \fBRetransformClasses\fR and a \fBClassFileLoadHook\fR callback.
The class file data is never modified, so the target application is not
redefined.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory.  Defaults to
\fIjvmdump\-<pid>\-<timestamp>\fR in the current directory, or in
\fI/tmp\fR when root dumps another user's JVM.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-include " " \fIGLOB\fR
Only dump classes whose dotted name matches \fIGLOB\fR.  The patterns
.B *
and
.B ?
are supported.  May be repeated or given comma separated.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIGLOB\fR
Skip classes matching \fIGLOB\fR.  May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-jdk
Exclude \fIjava.*\fR, \fIjavax.*\fR, \fIjdk.*\fR, \fIsun.*\fR, \fIcom.sun.*\fR,
\fIorg.w3c.*\fR and \fIorg.xml.*\fR.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Only list class names in \fI<out>/classes.txt\fR; do not write class files.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-flat
Write \fIcom.example.Foo.class\fR instead of \fIcom/example/Foo.class\fR.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-agent " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to \fIlibjvmdump.so\fR.  By default it is looked up next to the binary and
in the installation directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
How long to wait for the JVM to open its attach socket (default 10).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only the output path.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the complete agent report.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.I <out>/classes/
One \fI.class\fR file per loaded class.
.TP
.I <out>/manifest.tsv
Tab separated list of class name, size and relative file name.
.TP
.I <out>/failed.txt
Classes that JVMTI refused to retransform (usually hidden classes).
.TP
.I <out>/dump.log
Report written by the agent.  Contains \fIstatus: ok\fR on success.
.TP
.I <out>/classes.txt
Written in list mode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B jvmdump 1234
Dump every loaded class of process 1234 into a timestamped directory.
.TP
.B jvmdump \-\-no\-jdk \-o /tmp/dump 1234
Dump only application classes into \fI/tmp/dump\fR.
.TP
.B jvmdump \-l 1234 | grep Controller
List the loaded class names and filter them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 on invalid usage.
.SH NOTES
HotSpot only accepts attach requests from the JVM's own user.  When run as
root, \fBjvmdump\fR switches its effective uid/gid to the target process, and
the output directory must be writable by that user.
.PP
Hidden classes (lambdas and other runtime generated classes) are not
modifiable and cannot be retransformed; they are reported in
\fIfailed.txt\fR.
.PP
On recent JDKs the target JVM may need
\fI\-XX:+EnableDynamicAgentLoading\fR.  The agent can also be preloaded with
\fI\-agentpath:/usr/local/lib/jvmdump/libjvmdump.so=out=/tmp/dump,delay=10\fR;
\fIdelay=N\fR postpones the dump by N seconds after VM initialization.
.PP
JDK 21 and later print
\fIWARNING: A JVMTI agent has been loaded dynamically\fR to the target's
standard error.  HotSpot emits that message after opening the agent library
but before any agent code runs, so \fBjvmdump\fR redirects the target's
standard error to \fI/dev/null\fR for the few microseconds in between and
restores it at the start of \fIAgent_OnAttach\fR.  The warning therefore never
reaches the application's console and the application's own logging is not
affected.  The redirection is only used when the attach listener loads the
library; preloading with \fI\-agentpath\fR does not touch the descriptor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR javap (1),
.BR jcmd (1)
